#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d8dc0-98eb-53d0-9e48-3b1c2d7f6308" :question/math-academy-id "e-4508" :question/problem "Find a solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=2 \\\\ 4x+3y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/id #uuid "422d31ad-8caa-5ce2-a0e0-c905fcc2640d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4509" :question/problem "Solve the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 6y-5x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186291756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c963c1-98e9-5a2d-a5c7-0f6d04dbda30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291758} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c36bc2-4930-5d0c-9a5f-14d8dcb8f959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291759} {:answer/id #uuid "590404f5-f3f8-532b-aeb2-8ac76e440df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291760} {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} {:answer/id #uuid "850318a6-1a4d-5307-b80c-b8e0f486b5e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "796acc5c-1913-5743-9dd1-c48bcd03d333" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291761} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca356f0b-e266-5dae-b876-0c22bbf0bfe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95af1977-8d23-5d4e-89a9-245a921e273b" :question/math-academy-id "q-102806" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc9c5fb-366e-58cc-800c-cc96a8f541ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284736} {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1d318-b9c1-5dee-a68e-573efd3017fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284738} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ecfbe4-3a59-5c01-b930-32e7ac659265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{20}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284739} {:answer/id #uuid "58ddedb4-aea2-53f6-b4c4-c995257df447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01755979-0354-5a8c-8358-06db0e668a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284737} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ac07c7-8f78-5bfe-8981-b98603a3d774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "174955d4-f9c8-5173-abe1-fa5e22029d62" :question/math-academy-id "q-102809" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=1-3y \\\\ 3-4y=2x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+3y=1 \\\\ -2x-4y=-3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-4)-(-2)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092625 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf74a139-ec79-5146-acec-8db4355df6a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090232} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b491fa-3547-5fba-b7e4-a07ec08d7555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090233} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4fb44c-643c-5621-a968-e5e855c3228d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090234} {:answer/id #uuid "05ce90d3-dd9d-5cc1-90b9-3adb919bde81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090235} {:answer/id #uuid "1961679b-bcc9-512b-85dd-ea7ba1a134ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x =-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4fb44c-643c-5621-a968-e5e855c3228d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090234} :answer-field/id #uuid "db547192-1728-5daf-81fe-bde3526a1a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186090231}] :question/id #uuid "a6d30370-c2bc-519b-ba0f-95ca534628ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-31893" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n${x - 2y = 1; 2x + 2y =-1$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01681ac2-e161-567b-8a45-b934df1d456b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286343} {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5121d015-f1d8-52bf-9d65-0cea17480a9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286344} :answer-field/id #uuid "32cde33b-9de2-5a38-ab81-1e07d7256b1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286342} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cb5c507-528b-50a5-8985-9c5fa03c23e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286346} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5432b9-fedd-5640-9faf-47c1ca67c1e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286345} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2808ac36-e8ac-5295-9c1f-d84ef7b7493c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286348} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7f1347f-288e-5404-8433-c1128330b84b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1ccae0e-0d02-5cab-8336-a50181fa21a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-320805" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=7 \\\\ 5x+2y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93d5301e-cdac-549c-8b27-594042eb57ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93d5301e-cdac-549c-8b27-594042eb57ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41db4be-d748-5c7d-8931-5326da2c7d9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca77f706-eb7e-571a-bc3b-9e44b9fffd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca77f706-eb7e-571a-bc3b-9e44b9fffd37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284788} :answer-field/id #uuid "4462897a-eb59-5abc-b1f3-121e26a7dc7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9f28575-101d-5daa-b849-50e5193c23df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9f28575-101d-5daa-b849-50e5193c23df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284790} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5daf6a-5623-5507-8669-9845e20e3155" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "44824f47-f8c3-52d7-9631-687da781e31e" :question/math-academy-id "q-321439" :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x=3+y \\\\ 5y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $10$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $10$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+5y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
